Venetium 0041 - hardware H.264 decoding when ANGLE runs on Direct3D 9 (no D3D11 device), e.g. Windows ARM32 Tegra 3/4
(BATCH MEDIA-1). cr150 deleted the D3D9 DXVA decoder and D3D11VideoDecoder needs a D3D11 device ANGLE never has on arm, so every
codec was software-decoded. media::DXVAVideoDecoder ports Chromium 77's DXVAVideoDecodeAccelerator D3D9 path: CMSH264DecoderMFT
from msmpeg2vdec.dll (DllGetClassObject) + IDirect3DDeviceManager9 on ANGLE's own D3D9Ex device (D3DCREATE_MULTITHREADED), each
NV12 output StretchRect'ed into an X8R8G8B8 share-handle texture that ANGLE samples via an EGL pbuffer bound once to a GL texture
wrapped as a SharedImage (new GLTextureImageBacking::InitializeWithExternalPassthroughTexture + GpuChannelSharedImageInterface::
CreateSharedImageForD3D9Video). Per-device DXVA2 probe (H.264 VLD + NV12 + 1080p/720p config) decides support; any init failure
falls back to software. GpuMojoMediaClientWin uses it only when there is no D3D11 device (x86/x64 D3D11 paths unchanged) and
guards the D3D12 CHECK on a null device; mf_initializer preloads msmpeg2vdec.dll + dxva2.dll before the sandbox. Frames are XRGB
(opaque) with power_efficient set. Reports VideoDecoderType::kVda: chrome://media-internals shows VDAVideoDecoder.

